        <p>Song titles in gold link to a full story on this site.</p>
        <p>Year is the year-end Hot 100 the song appears on, and Year-End Rank is its place on that list.</p>
        <p>The #1 Hit column and every date in the last column come from the weekly Hot 100 number ones, not year-end rank.</p>


        <h2 id="answer">The Short Answer: What Makes a 70s Slow Song</h2>
        <p>A 70s slow song is a Hot 100 hit from 1970 to 1979 that sits at ballad pace and is tagged chill or reflect in this site's song data.</p>
        <p>The song data holds no tempo field, so "slow" is an editorial call, not a beats-per-minute count.</p>
        <p>Here is what the list shows at a glance:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>{{TOP_GENRE_N}} of the {{N}} songs carry the {{TOP_GENRE}} tag in this site's song data.</li>
          <li>{{TOP_MOOD_N}} of the {{N}} lead with a melancholy mood tag, so the decade's slow songs lean sad.</li>
          <li>The longest runs at number one are six weeks, held by "Bridge Over Troubled Water" and "Alone Again (Naturally)."</li>
          <li>{{N1}} songs reached number one, and {{NOT_N1}} stayed on the year-end lists only.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Not Sure Which Slow Song Fits the Moment?</h3>
        <p>The <a href="/pages/mood-song-matcher">Mood Song Matcher</a> works from this site's own mood tags.</p>
        <p>It is a quick way to sort the sad slow song from the sweet one before you press Play.</p>

        <h2 id="method">How These 70s Slow Songs Were Chosen</h2>
        <p>The starting pool came from this site's own song data.</p>
        <p>It tags every year-end Hot 100 song for 1970 to 1979 with a vibe.</p>
        <p>{{POOL}} songs are tagged chill or reflect and have a YouTube video on record.</p>
        <p>From that pool, {{N}} made the list on four tests:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Each year of the decade gets exactly three songs.</li>
          <li>The song is not already on the 70s party, dance, love or road trip songs lists.</li>
          <li>Its chart facts can be checked against the weekly or year-end Billboard data on this site.</li>
          <li>Its chart line is computed from that data, never typed from memory.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>{{OVERLAP}} songs in the slow pool already sit on those four companion lists, so they are left out here.</p>

        <h3>Where the Year-End Rank on These 70s Slow Songs Comes From</h3>
        <p>The Year-End Rank column is a position on that year's Billboard year-end list.</p>
        <p>It is not the song's weekly peak.</p>
        <p>"Time in a Bottle" sits at 24 for 1974, yet it reached number one on December 29, 1973.</p>
        <p>Rather than scroll, you can <a href="/radio/?play=1970-1-bridge-over-troubled-water">open the same songs on Listen Now</a> and let the jukebox run.</p>

        <h2 id="moods">Sad, Sweet or Looking Back: The Mood Mix</h2>
        <p>Every song in this site's data carries mood tags, and the first tag is the main one.</p>
        <p>Counting the first tag across the {{N}} songs shows what a slow song usually feels like.</p>

