        <h3>Melancholy Wins, and Wins at the Top</h3>
        <p>{{TOP_MOOD_N}} of the {{N}} songs lead with melancholy.</p>
        <p>{{MEL_N1}} of the {{N1}} number ones on the list are among them.</p>
        <p>That includes "Without You," "Alone Again (Naturally)" and "Sad Eyes."</p>
        <p>For the sweeter side of the decade, see the <a href="/blog/songs/70s-love-songs/">70s love songs</a> list.</p>

        <h3>James Taylor Appears Twice</h3>
        <p>James Taylor has two songs here, "Fire and Rain" and "You've Got a Friend."</p>
        <p>The first is number 67 on the 1970 year-end list.</p>
        <p>The second reached number one on July 31, 1971.</p>

        <h2 id="genres">Soft Rock and Soul: The Genre Mix</h2>
        <p>The genre tag in this site's song data splits the {{N}} songs four ways.</p>

        <div class="data-table-wrap">
          <table class="data-table">
            <caption>The {{N}} 70s slow songs by genre tag, with how many reached number one</caption>
